  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31404674",
      "title": "Publishing Apps: An Overview",
      "lectureOrder": 233,
      "videoOrder": 227,
      "sourceHash": "a6d6485a8f6acedbe2ef4e95974a64fc821dcbb3673bf03e97e862455cde6ad8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.32,
          "end": 4,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmüller] So, how do you publish",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4,
          "end": 5.49,
          "en": "React Native Apps?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.49,
          "end": 7.46,
          "en": "And just to be super clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.46,
          "end": 9.46,
          "en": "publishing apps means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.46,
          "end": 11.85,
          "en": "that we put them into the Google Play Store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.85,
          "end": 13.41,
          "en": "or the Apple App Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 13.41,
          "end": 16.593,
          "en": "That is what I mean when I say publish apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.6,
          "end": 19.56,
          "en": "Well, we have to differentiate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.56,
          "end": 22.33,
          "en": "between Expo Managed Apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.33,
          "end": 25.85,
          "en": "and React Native Apps that don't use Expo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.85,
          "end": 27.33,
          "en": "Now very important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.33,
          "end": 29.99,
          "en": "Expo Apps include both apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.99,
          "end": 31.71,
          "en": "that use the Managed Workflow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 31.71,
          "end": 33.54,
          "en": "or the Bare Workflow",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 33.54,
          "end": 37.24,
          "en": "about which I talked in the previous course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 37.24,
          "end": 39.71,
          "en": "So if you're using Expo in any way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 39.71,
          "end": 42.78,
          "en": "you can benefit from certain advantages as you will see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 42.78,
          "end": 44.3,
          "en": "If your not using Expo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 44.3,
          "end": 46.85,
          "en": "you can of course also build and publish your apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 46.85,
          "end": 48.82,
          "en": "but it is a bit more cumbersome",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 48.82,
          "end": 51.6,
          "en": "as you will see later in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 51.6,
          "end": 53.27,
          "en": "Now, if you're using Expo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 53.27,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "with the Managed or the Bare Workflow,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 59.52,
          "en": "it starts with configuring your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 59.52,
          "end": 62.92,
          "en": "Now there are tons of settings you can set as you will see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 62.92,
          "end": 66.85,
          "en": "but there are couple of key settings you should be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 66.85,
          "end": 68.28,
          "en": "Once you did that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 68.28,
          "end": 69.15,
          "en": "and this, by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 69.15,
          "end": 71.45,
          "en": "also includes things like adding icons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 71.45,
          "end": 72.99,
          "en": "But once you did that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 72.99,
          "end": 76.61,
          "en": "you can move on and build the actual App Binaries,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 76.61,
          "end": 80.53,
          "en": "the installable app files that can be installed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 80.53,
          "end": 82.77,
          "en": "on iOS or Android devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 82.77,
          "end": 84.39,
          "en": "And when using Expo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 84.39,
          "end": 89.2,
          "en": "you can use Expo's Cloud Build Service for free",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 89.2,
          "end": 92.56,
          "en": "which actually allows you to outsource that build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 92.56,
          "end": 95.7,
          "en": "to the servers provided by the Expo company",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 95.7,
          "end": 99.35,
          "en": "so that the build does not take place on your machine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 99.35,
          "end": 101.25999999999999,
          "en": "but on their machines instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 101.25999999999999,
          "end": 102.97,
          "en": "which of course means that you don't need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 102.97,
          "end": 105.1,
          "en": "to use your resources.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 105.1,
          "end": 107.37,
          "en": "If you have a slower computer, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 107.37,
          "end": 109,
          "en": "you don't have to use that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 109,
          "end": 112.71000000000001,
          "en": "And a great advantage of using this cloud service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 112.71000000000001,
          "end": 114.63,
          "en": "is also that Expo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 114.63,
          "end": 118.08,
          "en": "and their cloud service will build your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 118.08,
          "end": 121.7,
          "en": "for different platforms, for iOS and Android.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 121.7,
          "end": 125.99,
          "en": "At least if you want to build the app for both platforms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 125.99,
          "end": 128.36,
          "en": "If you would build the app locally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 128.36,
          "end": 131.13,
          "en": "you could not build an iOS app on Windows,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 131.13,
          "end": 135.1,
          "en": "for example, that's a restriction applied by Apple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 135.1,
          "end": 138.42000000000002,
          "en": "With the cloud service when using Expo's Cloud Service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 138.42000000000002,
          "end": 140.81,
          "en": "and building the app on their servers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 140.81,
          "end": 144.86,
          "en": "they will build both an iOS and an Android app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 144.86,
          "end": 146.173,
          "en": "in their respective environments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 146.173,
          "end": 149.381,
          "en": "and therefore you get apps for both platforms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 149.381,
          "end": 151.87,
          "en": "even if you don't own a Mac.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 151.87,
          "end": 155.11,
          "en": "So that can be a huge advantage here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 155.11,
          "end": 157.22,
          "en": "And then once the app was built,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 157.22,
          "end": 159.23,
          "en": "you can submit it to the app stores",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 159.23,
          "end": 161.99,
          "en": "either manually or even again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 161.99,
          "end": 165.43,
          "en": "by leveraging a certain service provided by Expo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 165.43,
          "end": 167.51,
          "en": "which makes this publishing process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 167.51,
          "end": 170.393,
          "en": "this submission process also seamless.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 171.37,
          "end": 173.12,
          "en": "So that's the Expo side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 173.12,
          "end": 176.043,
          "en": "Very simple as you will see, very convenient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 176.94,
          "end": 179.98,
          "en": "Without Expo, you also need to configure your project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 179.98,
          "end": 180.91,
          "en": "in a certain way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 180.91,
          "end": 185.31,
          "en": "and then you must build your App Binaries locally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 185.31,
          "end": 188.29,
          "en": "which means you have to build them on your machine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 188.29,
          "end": 191.9,
          "en": "You might also find other third party service providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 191.9,
          "end": 193.57,
          "en": "which offer a cloud build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 193.57,
          "end": 196.46,
          "en": "but you can't use Expo's Cloud Build Service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 196.46,
          "end": 199.03,
          "en": "if you're not using a Expo project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 199.03,
          "end": 202.45,
          "en": "at least not at the point of time where I'm recording this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 202.45,
          "end": 205.46,
          "en": "So you then must build your App Binaries locally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 205.46,
          "end": 208.153,
          "en": "And in case of iOS apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 208.153,
          "end": 210.76,
          "en": "that means that you need a Mac device",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 210.76,
          "end": 213.21,
          "en": "because otherwise as mentioned multiple times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 213.21,
          "end": 215.313,
          "en": "you can't build iOS apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 216.17000000000002,
          "end": 218.62,
          "en": "And then again, you can submit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 218.62,
          "end": 220.51,
          "en": "those built App Binaries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 220.51,
          "end": 224.27,
          "en": "to the respective app stores manually in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 224.27,
          "end": 226.82999999999998,
          "en": "since we're not using Expo's Cloud Service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 226.82999999999998,
          "end": 229.67000000000002,
          "en": "So therefore this auto submission service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 229.67000000000002,
          "end": 232.633,
          "en": "which I will show you later will not be available here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 233.77,
          "end": 235.26,
          "en": "So these are the differences,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 235.26,
          "end": 237.26,
          "en": "you can build apps either way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 237.26,
          "end": 239.99,
          "en": "It will be a bit more convenient with Expo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 239.99,
          "end": 240.94,
          "en": "but in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 240.94,
          "end": 243.063,
          "en": "I will show you both approaches.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
